## 6. ADVANCE semantics

[SPECIFIED]

Advance chooses a later block index under the current monotone-sweep
constraint.

Direct backward movement is not an allowed ADVANCE operation.

## 7. REPEAT semantics

[SPECIFIED]

REPEAT executes the current block again at the current block index.

## 8. RESTART semantics

[SPECIFIED]

RESTART returns the block pointer to the beginning of the sweep while
preserving the live hidden state.

It is a scheduling transition, not a reset of the reasoning state.

## 9. HALT semantics

[SPECIFIED]

HALT terminates the current within-token computation and proceeds to the
terminal state-update / output stage.

## 10. Execution-mask constraints

[PARTIALLY SPECIFIED]

The canonical design requires legal-action masking consistent with:

- monotone forward ADVANCE
- valid block indices
